---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { brokers, otherBrokers, voteGuide } from "../data/brokers";
---

<Base
  title="How to vote"
  description="Broker-by-broker voting steps from Tesla’s shareholder vote guide, with a clear note that no combination proxy has been filed."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">No combination ballot exists yet</p>
      <h1>How TSLA shares get voted.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A combination would be voted only after a proxy names a record date and a meeting. This
        page collects the company’s own broker instructions so holders know the path. It does not
        invent menu clicks the company did not publish.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Do not reuse an old control number.</strong>
          Tesla’s vote guide, retrieved October 24, 2026, tells holders to search for emails
          received in 2025 and refers to a September 15 record date. It does not say which year
          that September 15 was. The December 3, 2026 annual meeting has its own proxy, filed
          October 19, 2026. A later combination would have another one.
        </p>
        <p class="source">
          <a href={voteGuide.href}>Tesla shareholder vote guide</a> · retrieved {voteGuide.asOf}<br />
          <a href="https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1318605/000110465926116716/tm267596d6_defa14a.htm">DEFA14A</a>
          · 2026 annual meeting on December 3, 2026 · proxy filed October 19, 2026
        </p>
      </div>
      <h2>Before the broker list</h2>
      <ul class="clean">
        <li>You vote the shares you held on the record date printed in that meeting’s proxy. Shares bought after the record date are not in that vote.</li>
        <li>Shares inside a mutual fund or ETF are voted by the manager unless the fund offers a pass-through program. See <a href="/holders/">Who holds TSLA</a>.</li>
        <li>A standing instruction under the <a href="/retail-voting-program/">retail voting program</a> can vote a future meeting with the board. It does not vote the December 3, 2026 annual meeting. Option 2 leaves mergers to you.</li>
        <li>If no instructions arrive, Tesla’s guide says to ask the broker whether it offers proxy voting. Some brokers outside the United States do not.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The guide lists {voteGuide.solicitor} at {voteGuide.phoneUs} from the United States or Canada
        and {voteGuide.phoneIntl} from elsewhere, for questions about how to vote. Those numbers are
        the ones printed on that page as of {voteGuide.asOf}.
      </p>
    </section>

    <h2>Broker by broker</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Each block is Tesla’s published instruction, not a separate walkthrough. Webull is absent from
      the company’s list, so that card points at the “all other brokers” steps.
    </p>
    <div class="grid-2">
      {
        brokers.map((broker) => (
          <article class="broker">
            <p class="kicker">{broker.inTeslaGuide ? "On Tesla’s guide" : "Not on Tesla’s guide"}</p>
            <h3>{broker.name}</h3>
            <ol class="steps">
              {broker.steps.map((step) => (
                <li>{step}</li>
              ))}
            </ol>
            <p class="source">
              <a href={voteGuide.href}>Tesla vote guide</a> · retrieved {voteGuide.asOf}
            </p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>All other brokers</h2>
      <p>Tesla’s guide says to try these searches in email received in 2025:</p>
      <ul class="clean">
        {otherBrokers.map((step) => <li>{step}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p>
        Schwab’s card is the only one where the company’s guide also describes voting inside the
        brokerage site and at proxyvote.com with a 16-digit control number. For the other named
        brokers, the published step is the email.
      </p>
      <p><a class="button" href={voteGuide.href}>Open Tesla’s vote guide</a></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
